Generating Pytest & Allure Reports:
-----------------------------------
- playwright-python doesn't have the native support feature to generate reports.
  Where as playwright-typescript and playwright-javascript does support.
- So we generate reports using pytest.
- Also allure reports are popular now a days and used for report generation using python.
- So to generate the reports we need to download plugins:
        - pytest-html plugin
        --------------------
                * step-1: Install the plugin [pip install pytest-html]
                * step-2: Configure pytest.ini
                            [pytest]
                            addopts = --headed
                                      --browser=chromium
                                      --video=retain-on-failure
                                      --screenshot=only-on-failure
                                      --tracing=retain-on-failure
                                      --html=myreport.html --self-contained-html --capture=tee-sys

                * step-3: Create sample tests
                * step-4: Run the tests and generate report.
                * step-5: Attach screenshots on Test Failure (conftest.py) - additional steps

        - Allure reports
        -----------------
                * step-1: Install Allure Pytest plugin [pip install allure-Pytest]
                * step-2: Install Allure Command-Line Tool (to view and generate reports)
                          windows: https://github.com/allure-framework/allure2/releases
                * step-3: Configure Allure in pytest.ini
                          --alluredir=PlaywrightWithPython/allurereports/allure-results
                * step-4: Create and Run your test.
                * step-5: Generate and View the Allure Reports
                * step-6: Attach screenshots on test failures (conftest.py)


